From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Pitkin <robpitkin@google.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:43:51 -0700
Subject: hid: Prevent UAF in OnPermissionRevoked

WebViewChooserContext::OnPermissionRevoked iterated over
origins_per_device while synchronously notifying observers via
chooser_context_->PermissionForWebViewRevoked(guest_origin).

When a <webview> guest shares its embedder's origin, the re-entrant
OnPermissionRevoked notification erases the device entry that the outer
iterator was pointing to. When the outer call resumes, it operates on
the deallocated std::map node, causing a heap use-after-free and
double-free in the browser process.

Fix this by collecting the revoked guest origins and erasing the device
map entries prior to notifying observers, ensuring no live iterators to
device_access_ are held across re-entrant notifications. This matches
the erase-first ordering in RevokeDevicePermission and
RevokeEphemeralPermissions.

Additionally, revoke WebView device grants when GetDeviceInfo() returns
nullptr (for example, during HidChooserContext::DeviceRemoved where
devices_ is updated before notifying observers) instead of skipping
them.

Bug: 574199198
Change-Id: I64b9102188d7099a8093516173dc80684a99ae69
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8592406
Reviewed-by: Alvin Ji <alvinji@chromium.org>
